Licensing recommendation for this repository
============================================

This repository combines two kinds of material, and the recommended
open-licensing structure treats them separately:

1. Textbook prose, figures, and exercises (everything under book/ and
   figures/ except code):

   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   CC BY 4.0 is the license used by OpenStax Calculus, which this book
   cites, and it is the standard for open educational resources (OER).
   It permits reuse, adaptation, and redistribution with attribution.
   If the department prefers to restrict commercial reuse, CC BY-NC-SA
   4.0 is a common alternative, at the cost of no longer being a fully
   open OER license.

2. Source code (Python scripts, notebook code cells, build tooling):

   MIT License

   Code embedded in an educational work should carry a simple permissive
   license so students may reuse snippets freely in their own work.

Before public release, replace this file with the chosen license text
(or a LICENSE plus LICENSE-CODE pair) and add a copyright line naming
the university and authors. No third-party figures or datasets are
included in this repository; all figures are generated by original
scripts in figures/scripts/.
